cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, and also cite the original reference-equation paper(s) you used (see references.bib)."
type: software
title: "pyios: Reference equations for impulse oscillometry"
abstract: >-
  pyios calculates predicted values, percent predicted, z-scores and lower/upper limits of
  normal for impulse oscillometry (IOS) parameters using five published reference equation
  sets (Moitra 2020, Oostveen 2013, Schulz 2013, Berger 2021, Gochicoa-Rangel 2023).
  It provides a Python package (pyios) and an R port (rios) with identical behaviour.
